16:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"When treatment goals shift to comfort, PCT work becomes central rather than supporting. Nothing else is being done, and the quality of a person's final days rests substantially on the care they receive at the bedside."}]
17:["$","figure","2",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Need"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Care"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Mouth care"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Frequent moistening; mouths dry quickly and it is a major source of discomfort"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Positioning"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Reposition gently for comfort rather than on a rigid schedule"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Skin and linens"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Clean and dry; change promptly"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Environment"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Quiet, dim, uncluttered; support family presence"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Pain"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Report signs promptly — grimacing, restlessness, guarding"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Presence"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Sit with them; hearing is thought to persist late"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Comfort care priorities"}]]}]
18:["$","div","3",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-blue-50 border-blue-400","children":[false,"Speak to a dying patient as though they can hear you, because they may. Introduce yourself, explain what you are doing, and avoid conversation across them that you would not want them to hear. Families notice this, and it matters to them long afterwards."]}]
19:["$","p","4",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Practices around death vary considerably between cultures and religions — who may be present, who may touch the body, whether it should be washed and by whom, which direction it should face, how quickly burial must occur. Do not assume based on someone's background. Ask the family what they need and what they would like you to do differently, and pass it to the nurse."}]
1a:["$","figure","5",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Do"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Avoid"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Say 'I'm sorry' and mean it"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"'They're in a better place' — assumes beliefs they may not hold"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Offer specific practical help"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"'Let me know if you need anything' — nobody follows up on this"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Allow silence"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Filling it out of your own discomfort"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Say 'I don't know, but I'll ask the nurse'"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Guessing at prognosis or clinical questions"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Let them talk about the person"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Changing the subject to spare yourself"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Communicating with families"}]]}]
1b:["$","div","6",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Compassion fatigue and burnout are occupational hazards of this work, not personal weaknesses. The signs are emotional numbness, dreading shifts, irritability, sleep disturbance, and losing the empathy that brought you here. It is cumulative and it responds to being addressed early. Use whatever your employer offers — debriefs, employee assistance, peer support — and take the time you are owed. Staff who never acknowledge this are the ones who leave the profession."]}]
1c:["$","$L20","7",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"A family member of a dying patient says 'I don't know how to do this.' What is the most appropriate response?","options":["'They're in a better place now.'","Acknowledge how hard it is, allow silence, and offer something specific — a chair, a blanket, time alone with them","'Everything happens for a reason.'","Change the subject to something lighter to distract them"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"They are expressing distress rather than asking a question. Acknowledgment, silence, and a concrete offer of help are more useful than reassurance — and phrases that impose a belief or a meaning often land badly with someone who does not share them.","optionRationales":["This assumes religious beliefs the family may not hold, and can feel dismissive.","Correct. Acknowledge, allow silence, and offer something specific and practical.","This imposes a framework on their grief and frequently causes offence.","Distraction communicates that their distress is unwelcome."]}}]
1d:["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl","children":"Apply what you've learned in this lesson."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"This is worth thinking through before you are in the room."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Research the physical signs that death is approaching, and what families are commonly told to expect."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Research end-of-life practices in three religious or cultural traditions. Note what would need to be accommodated."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Write three things you could say to a grieving family member, and three to avoid, with your reasoning."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Identify what support your employer or program offers for staff after a patient death, and note how to access it before you need to."}]]}]]}]}]]}]
